  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, the number of real roots of the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><strong>Case 1</strong></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>140</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>141</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>141</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>We know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>141</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, both roots lie in the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><strong>Case 2</strong></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#8746;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>We know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>So, both roots lie in the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#8746;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;real roots.</p>",
